#### lambda_expression
SYNTAX: §LAM{id:param:type...} expression §/LAM{id}
DESC: Creates an anonymous function/lambda expression. The id is required. Lambda parameters are name:type pairs after the id. Can capture variables from enclosing scope.
  C#: x => x * 2
  CAL: §LAM{lam1:x:i32} (* x 2) §/LAM{lam1}
  C#: (a, b) => a + b
  CAL: §LAM{lam1:a:i32:b:i32} (+ a b) §/LAM{lam1}
  C#: items.Where(x => x > 5)
  CAL: §C{items.Where} §A §LAM{lam1:x:i32} (> x 5) §/LAM{lam1} §/C

#### field_definition
SYNTAX: §FLD{type:name:visibility}
DESC: Defines a field in a class. Usually private, prefixed with underscore by convention.
  C#: private string _name;
  CAL: §FLD{str:_name:priv}
  C#: private readonly int _id;
  CAL: §FLD{i32:_id:priv:readonly}

#### constructor
SYNTAX: §CTOR{id:vis} (type:param, ...)
DESC: Defines a class constructor. Use §BASE with §A arguments to call a base constructor, or §THIS to chain constructors.
  C#: public User(string name) { _name = name; }
  CAL: §CTOR{ctor001:pub} (str:name)
  §ASSIGN _name name
  C#: public Admin(string name) : base(name) { }
  CAL: §CTOR{ctor001:pub} (str:name)
  §BASE §A name
